  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(\\theta\\) is an acute angle and \\[ \\sin\\frac12\\theta=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{2x}}, \\] then \\(\\tan\\theta\\) equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac1x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x-1}}{x+1}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{x^2-1}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1973-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The half-angle identity gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\cos\\theta &=1-2\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ &=1-\\frac{x-1}{x}\\\\ &=\\frac1x. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore \\[ \\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta-1=x^2-1. \\] Because \\(\\theta\\) is acute, its tangent is positive, so \\[ \\tan\\theta=\\sqrt{x^2-1}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(\\cos\\theta=1-2\\sin^2(\\frac{\\theta}{2})\\)",
        "Once \\(\\cos\\theta\\) is known, apply \\(\\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta-1\\) and use that \\(\\theta\\) is acute"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
